WEBVTT

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:11.293
WindLab · choose the wind approach and inspect ULS wall pressures.

00:00:11.293 --> 00:00:15.753
Shared-column extension · add a right-hand skillion roof to the existing bay.

00:00:15.753 --> 00:00:19.143
The extension is 3.0 m wide. Select the main end wall for the door.

00:00:19.143 --> 00:00:27.409
Opening editor · enter a 2.0 m door width and apply the revised framing.

00:00:27.409 --> 00:00:29.034
Recalculate the edited shed with the current WindLab pressures.

00:00:29.034 --> 00:00:40.540
Wind 3D · follow the east-wind ULS pressures from WindLab onto the edited shed surfaces.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:01:02.079
Portal analysis · select the frame and load combination. Read bending, shear and displacement.

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:08.600
Trace the force path from the windward surface through the roof and wall braces to the bases.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:14.753
Bracing · compare axial strap resistance and the screw-group resistance at each end.

00:01:14.753 --> 00:01:20.843
Wall panel SH-024 · 7.96 kN along the bay. The calculation counts one active tension diagonal.

00:01:20.843 --> 00:01:44.378
Connections · review the simultaneous forces at a column base, then inspect the joint model.

00:01:44.378 --> 00:01:49.405
Review the joint assumptions, fixing capacities and outstanding checks before engineering approval.
